# Citation metadata in the Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# Two separate lists: `authors` are the people who wrote the software, whom
# Zenodo credits when a release is archived; `preferred-citation` is the paper,
# with its own authors, which GitHub shows under "Cite this repository".
# Add a line under `authors` for each new contributor.
cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
title: "CNETA: Copy Number Evolutionary Tree Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Programs to simulate copy number alterations along a phylogenetic tree
  (cnets) and to infer the phylogenetic tree, node ages and mutation rates
  from the copy number profiles of multiple samples of one patient, by
  maximum likelihood (cnetml) or by MCMC (cnetmcmc).
authors:
  - family-names: Lu
    given-names: Bingxin
repository-code: "https://github.com/lu-cbio-group/cneta2"
url: "https://lu-cbio-group.github.io/cneta2/"
license: GPL-3.0
message: >-
  If you use CNETA, please cite the CNETML paper below and this repository.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "CNETML: maximum likelihood inference of phylogeny from copy number profiles of multiple samples"
  authors:
    - family-names: Lu
      given-names: Bingxin
    - family-names: Curtius
      given-names: Kit
    - family-names: Graham
      given-names: Trevor A.
    - family-names: Yang
      given-names: Ziheng
    - family-names: Barnes
      given-names: Chris P.
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9459-1395"
  journal: Genome Biology
  volume: 24
  issue: 1
  start: 144
  year: 2023
  doi: 10.1186/s13059-023-02983-0
